<section>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>The comeback has a clock</h2>
      <p>If current policies stay in place, a 2023 UN-backed assessment projects a return to 1980 ozone levels at different times.</p>
      <smart-layout orientation="horizontal" variant="minimalTimeline">
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Around 2040 · Global</h4>
          <p>Ozone levels across most of the world could return first.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Around 2045 · Arctic</h4>
          <p>Recovery near the North Pole is projected a little later.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Around 2066 · Antarctic</h4>
          <p>Recovery near the South Pole is expected to take longest.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
      </smart-layout>
      <aside variant="success"><p>These are projections, not guaranteed dates. Continuing the plan matters.</p></aside>
      <p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP, 2023 assessment</a></p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>